menu "Gateway: storage"

    config GW_EMU_NO_PSRAM
        bool
        default y if GW_IO_SIMULATED && !SPIRAM
        help
            Issue #135: the firmware assumes the 8 MB of PSRAM of the board. A board whose
            PSRAM is not detected boots in the fault mode only (network, web server and
            shell report the fault; the gateway does not start). This hidden option is set
            only in the QEMU build without PSRAM (sdkconfig.qemu: CONFIG_GW_IO_SIMULATED and
            no CONFIG_SPIRAM). There the gateway runs from internal RAM, with the small
            sizes of CONFIG_GW_SPB_PAYLOAD_INTERNAL and CONFIG_GW_SF_SAMPLES, for the E2E
            scenarios that do not depend on memory (they run faster without PSRAM).

    config GW_CONFIG_MAX_BYTES
        int "Largest accepted /cfg/config.json (bytes)"
        range 4096 1048576
        default 131072
        help
            The spec maximum (16 devices, 256 tags with every field) is about 46 KB of
            compact JSON and 82 KB indented with 2 spaces. The file and the parser's
            document tree (about 200 KB for 256 tags) are allocated at boot, in PSRAM,
            and freed before the gateway starts. A larger file is
            rejected: the gateway then stays stopped with the configuration error state.

    choice GW_SF_SPILL
        prompt "Store & forward spill (SPB-14, sparkplug.store_forward.sd)"
        default GW_SF_SPILL_SDMMC
        help
            Where the store & forward ring spills when it is full, if the configuration
            enables it (off by default). GPIO45, the card's D0, is a strapping pin: see
            docs/reference/store-and-forward.md#the-microsd-card-and-gpio45 before enabling it
            on a board.

        config GW_SF_SPILL_SDMMC
            bool "microSD card on SDMMC, 1-bit (CLK 48, CMD 47, D0 45)"

        config GW_SF_SPILL_LITTLEFS
            bool "A directory of the LittleFS partition (QEMU stand-in for the card)"

        config GW_SF_SPILL_NONE
            bool "None"
    endchoice

endmenu
